  "body_html": "<h1>Game Tree</h1>\n<p>The tree of a finite perfect-information extensive game is a finite connected\ndirected acyclic graph with a distinguished origin $\\theta$. Every non-origin node\nhas a unique predecessor, and iterating predecessors eventually reaches $\\theta$.</p>\n<p>Terminal nodes are those with no successors. Decision positions are nonterminal\nnodes. Each decision position has a nonempty successor set.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 6.2.1] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. Tree of nodes, origin, predecessor map, terminal nodes, and successors.</li>\n</ul>",
